1. Definitions

1.1 "Software" means the Status Player Minecraft mod, including its compiled
    JAR files, source code, assets, documentation and any part of them.

1.2 "Original Project" means the Status Player project published by the Author
    at https://github.com/Teufel2211/Status-Player.

1.3 "Release" means any version of the Original Project that the Author has
    published publicly, for example on Modrinth, CurseForge or GitHub Releases.

1.4 "Rebranding" means changing, removing or obscuring the name "Status Player",
    the mod identifier "statusmod", the Author's credits, or presenting the
    Software, or a modified version of it, as an independent work of your own.

2. What you may do

2.1 You may use and run the Software, including on your own Minecraft servers,
    including servers you monetize, without paying anything.

2.2 You may make copies of the Software for private use, for backups, and for
    installing it on servers and clients you operate.

2.3 You may modify the Software for private use. Private use means that neither
    the modified Software nor anything derived from it is distributed or
    published.

2.4 You may distribute complete, unmodified copies of the Software, provided
    that (a) the copy is not modified in any way, (b) it keeps the name
    "Status Player" and the mod identifier "statusmod", (c) this license is
    included, and (d) you do not claim authorship of the Software.

3. What you may not do

3.1 You may not rebrand the Software.

3.2 You may not publish, upload or distribute a modified version of the
    Software, or a version derived from it, unless Section 4 applies.

3.3 You may not remove, alter or hide copyright notices, author credits,
    license notices or build identifiers contained in the Software.

3.4 You may not use the name, logo or other branding of the Author in a way
    that suggests the Author endorses, sponsors or is responsible for your
    version.

4. Continuation after the project has been abandoned

4.1 If the Original Project has had no Release for at least twelve (12)
    consecutive months, you may publish a modified version of the Software
    ("Continuation") under the conditions of this section.

4.2 A Continuation may carry its own name. Rebranding is permitted for
    Continuations only.

4.3 A Continuation must clearly state, both in its project description and in
    its in-game mod metadata, that it is based on Status Player, and must link
    to the Original Project.

4.4 A Continuation must not claim the original work as its own and must not
    suggest that the Author endorses or is responsible for it.

4.5 This license continues to apply to every part of the Software contained in
    a Continuation. You may license your own additions under any terms, as long
    as those terms do not restrict the rights granted here for the inherited
    parts.

4.6 The twelve-month period is measured from the date of the most recent
    Release of the Original Project.

5. Termination

5.1 Any breach of this license ends all rights granted to you under it.

5.2 On termination you must stop using, distributing and publishing the
    Software and destroy the copies you hold, except where a statutory right
